Attention: Current changes in IF and Switch: currently the node has version 2.2 for IF and version 3.3 for Switch, there are 4 operation: greaterThan, lessThan are now changed to gt and lt, greaterThanEquals is changed to gte and lessThenEquals is changed to lte. The structure of writing type number, the value must be of the type 2.0. type: date has been changed to type: dateTime. boolean has added operations like true, false, exists, notExists, empty, notEmpty, notEquals

In n8n, the way to determine the branch (type: true/false) of an If node is based on the array position in the field connections[""].main — that is, the order of the sub-arrays inside main if true first and false second.

Every node in workflow must have it "name", it will use that "name" in connnection "node". Examples: "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "triggerAtHour": 14,
              "triggerAtMinute": 30
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "name": "Schedule Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "id": "ea849bed-d860-47cd-9d09-2fcec41062e4",
      "position": [
        -2448,
        1744
      ]
    },

